    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Multi Connect allows you to connect your WordPress site to the Multi platform for centralized management and updates. This plugin serves as a secure bridge between your WordPress installation and the Multi dashboard.</p>\n<p>Key Features:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Centralized site management</li>\n<li>Secure connection to Multi Wp platform</li>\n<li>Easy updates management</li>\n<li>Site monitoring capabilities</li>\n<li>Streamlined maintenance</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin files to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/multi-connect</code> directory, or install the plugin through the WordPress plugins screen.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; screen in WordPress.</li>\n<li>Visit the Multi Connect settings page to configure your connection.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='is%20this%20plugin%20secure%3F'>\nIs this plugin secure?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes, Multi Connect uses secure authentication methods and encrypted communications to ensure your site&#8217;s security.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='what%20wordpress%20versions%20are%20supported%3F'>\nWhat WordPress versions are supported?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>The plugin supports WordPress 5.8 and above.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Connect and manage multiple WordPress sites from a central dashboard with Multi Connect.",
